# ── Runtime state files (generated at runtime, not committed) ──────────────────
run-state.json
run-events.ndjson
orchestrator-log.ndjson
harness-audit.ndjson
eval-trigger.txt
sprint-contract.md
sprint-fence.json
/scope-classification.json
.sprintfoundry/
claude-progress.txt
eval-result-*.md
quality-gate-*.md
contract-tampered.flag
CHANGELOG.md
VERSION

# ── Project-under-test output (created by init.sh) ───────────────────────────
node_modules/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
dist/
build/
*.pyc

# ── Legacy example files at root (moved to examples/) ────────────────────────
# These are kept tracked for backward-compat but prefer examples/ directory
*.example.json
*.example.ndjson
*.example.md

# ── OS / editor ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.swp
.env

# Build artifacts / temp dirs
plugins/plugins_tmp/
.claude/worktrees/

# ── Local-only agent/skill mirrors ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The plugin source of truth is plugins/sprintfoundry/{agents,skills}/, and
# .claude/agents/ is held identical to it by scripts/check-agent-sync.sh.
# These two extra copies are local conveniences that nothing syncs or ships;
# tracking them would keep alive the four-copy drift problem recorded in
# docs/harness-engineering-review.md.
.agents/
.codex/

# ── Local assistant / tool scratch state ─────────────────────────────────────
.workbuddy/

# ── Superseded diagram ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The authoritative architecture diagram is the mermaid block in README.md,
# which renders on GitHub and cannot drift from a separately maintained image.
docs/architecture-flow.svg

# ── Binary build artifacts (released via GitHub Releases, not committed) ──────
*.plugin
*.skill

# ── Runtime log files already tracked — run these to untrack: ────────────────
# git rm --cached run-state.json run-events.ndjson orchestrator-log.ndjson harness-audit.ndjson
